or triangle \\( ABC \\)\nNow, let's assume \\( ABD \\) is a right triangle with \\( AB = 19 \\) and \\( BD = 16 \\). Then:\n\\[\nAD = \\sqrt{AB^2 - BD^2} = \\sqrt{19^2 - 16^2} = \\sqrt{361 - 256} = \\sqrt{105}\n\\]\n\n### Step 6: Calculate \\( BC \\) using Pythagorean theorem in triangle \\( ABC \\)\nNow, we use the Pythagorean theorem in triangle \\( ABC \\):\n\\[\nAB^2 + AC^2 = BC^2\n\\]\nSubstitute the given values:\n\\[\n16^2 + 37^2 = BC^2\n\\]\nCalculate each term:\n\\[\n16^2 = 256\n\\]\n\\[\n37^2 = 1369\n\\]\nAdd the squares:\n\\[\n256 + 1369 = 1625\n\\]\nThus:\n\\[\nBC^2 = 1625\n\\]\nTake the square root of both sides:\n\\[\nBC = \\sqrt{1625} = 5\\sqrt{65}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the length of segment \\( BC \\) is \\(\\boxed{37}\\).",
