.\n\n   The area of triangle \\( ABC \\) can be calculated in two ways:\n   - Using the base and height: \\( \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times AB \\times BC \\)\n   - Using the hypotenuse and height: \\( \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times AC \\times BC \\)\n\n   Equating the two areas:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{2} \\times 16 \\times x = \\frac{1}{2} \\times AC \\times x\n   \\]\n   Simplifying:\n   \\[\n   16 \\times x = AC \\times x\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   AC = 16\n   \\]\n\n8. **Verify the value of \\( x \\):**\n   Using the Pythagorean theorem in \\( BC \\):\n   \\[\n   AC^2 = 256 + x^2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   16^2 = 256 + x^2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   256 = 256 + x^2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x^2 = 0\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x = 12\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the length of segment \\( BC \\) is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).",
